  "yields": "Out of 10596 public incident reports, 7579 clearly say whether data was exposed and 5398 say how many records were lost. CyCRS learns how breaches happen from these rows and measures breach size on a log scale so one giant leak does not distort the picture for a small business.",
  "feeds": [],
  "limitations": [
    "Only 87 incidents are confirmed No disclosure, so the breach classifier has very few negatives.",
    "688 incidents have no confidentiality section and are left out of the target.",
    "VCDB is built from public news reports, so large and US organisations are over represented.",
    "VERIS Small (up to 1000 staff) cannot be split and is counted as small.",
    "Discovery time in days is known for only 1436 incidents."
  ]
